[17.753141, "o", "2. Download the LoRA adapter '\"'\"'dominguesm/xlm-roberta-base-lora-language-detection'\"'\"' \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 3. Configure the base model with 20 language classes (not the default 2)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 4. Save the configured model and tokenizer to '\"'\"'/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 5. Apply the LoRA adapter to the base model\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 6. Merge the LoRA adapter with the base model and save the merged model to '\"'\"'/app/merged_model/'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 7. Test language detection on the following 10 test samples and save results to '\"'\"'/app/detection_results.json'\"'\"':\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Note: The merged model will be evaluated for accuracy and must achieve at least 95% accuracy on a hidden multilingual test set (at least 75% per-language accuracy).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> You are not allowed to know the exact class IDs, directly use the argmax of the model'\"'\"'s output logits as the predicted_class_id.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> If the LoRA adapter is "]
[17.75322, "o", "applied correctly, the model will output the correct logits and achieve very high accuracy on the test samples.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The class IDs are intentionally hidden to prevent cheating; the evaluation will validate them automatically.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Test Samples:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"Bonjour, comment allez-vous aujourd'\"'\"'hui?\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"Hola, ¿cómo estás hoy?\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"Guten Tag, wie geht es Ihnen?\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"Ciao, come stai oggi?\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"Olá, como você está?\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"Привет, как дела?\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"こんにちは、お元気ですか？\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"你好，你好吗？\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"مرحبا، كيف حالك؟\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - \"Hello, how are you?\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Expected output format in detection_results.json:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ```json\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     \"text\": "]
[17.753263, "o", "\"input text\",\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     \"predicted_class_id\": 0,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     \"confidence\": 0.95\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   }\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ```'; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[174.105697, "o", "\r\n`test_setup_language_detection.py` — 11 tests, specified from the task text (argmax identity, output key set, error on length mismatch), not from the implementation body.\r\n\r\nVerified, not assumed:\r\n\r\n```\r\n11 passed, 0 failed        # PYTHONPATH shim, since pytest isn't installable offline\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe suite bites — I broke the code three ways and confirmed red each time:\r\n\r\n| Mutation | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| argmax → always index 0 | 5 failed |\r\n| naive softmax (no max subtraction) | 2 failed |\r\n| length check removed | 1 failed |\r\n| restored | 11 passed |\r\n\r\nOne honest finding: my first run had a genuine failure — I asserted `rel_tol=1e-9` against a confidence the implementation rounds to 6 dp. The implementation was right (the spec's `0.95` implies rounding) and my tolerance was tighter than the contract permits, so I stated the tolerance explicitly (`abs_tol=1e-6`) rather than loosening it to whatever passed.\r\n\r\n`python3 setup_language_detection.py --check` reports the exact blockers:\r\n\r\n```\r\nver"]
[174.10573, "o", "dict: NOT READY\r\n  -> install deps: pip install -r requirements.txt\r\n  -> model weights cannot be downloaded; grant network access\r\n```\r\n\r\n## To finish\r\n\r\n```\r\n/network on\r\npip install -r requirements.txt\r\npython3 setup_language_detection.py          # runs steps 1-7 end to end\r\npython3 -m pytest -q test_setup_language_detection.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nI can't promise the ≥95% accuracy threshold from here — that depends on the adapter actually aligning with a 20-class head, which only the hidden test set can confirm. The step ordering above is what gives it the best chance.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=24 surface=a825037b110a\r\n"]
